-----BEGIN PGP PUBLIC KEY PLACEHOLDER-----

This file will contain the armored PGP public key for
`security@craton.com.ar` once Craton's offline key-ceremony has been completed
(see SUPPLY_CHAIN.md#security-pgp-key-ceremony).

Until then, this placeholder exists intentionally so that:

  1. The path referenced from SECURITY.md resolves to a committed file
     (rather than 404-ing, which would make SECURITY.md look broken).
  2. Any future substitution of the file is visible in `git log` as a
     content change rather than as a file creation, making key-
     substitution attacks easier to detect.

If you are a security reporter and you need to send encrypted mail *now*,
please email `security@craton.com.ar` in plaintext and request a key;
an engineer will arrange an out-of-band secure channel.

-----END PGP PUBLIC KEY PLACEHOLDER-----
